  },
  {
   "text": "For example in a nativity the longitude of the Moon (Chandraspasta) is 11-",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    262,
    553,
    277
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "20-37-21 and the stretch of Revti Nakshatra being from 11-16-40 to 12-0-0:",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    286,
    510,
    302
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Longitude of the Moon 11-20-37",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    310,
    306,
    326
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Commencement of Revti 11-16-40",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    334,
    316,
    350
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Elapsed portion of Revti 3-57-21",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    358,
    306,
    374
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "By referring to the above table we will find that the 17th part ended at 3-46-",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    383,
    552,
    398
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "40 and the 18th part will end at 4-0-0. Therefore by the elapsing of 17th part the ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    407,
    556,
    422
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "effect of its Chandrakriya viz one. Who studies vedas' will be taken into account ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    431,
    556,
    446
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "which means that the native will be a learned person.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    455,
    382,
    471
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "<b>Chandra Avastha</b>",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    479,
    225,
    495
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "For finding out Chandra Avastha the stretch of a Nakshatra has to be divided ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    503,
    556,
    519
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "into 12 parts. Thus one part will come to 1-6-40.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    528,
    357,
    543
   ]
  },
